--------------------------------------------------------------------
Technology acknowledgements

Clio Coder builds on Earendil Works' Pi framework and, for optional Claude
workers, Anthropic's Claude Agent SDK. Its runtime and development tools
include Node.js, TypeScript, node-pty, Tree-sitter, Ollama's JavaScript
client, esbuild, tsup, and Biome. The source GUI uses React, Deno, Vite,
and community libraries for Markdown, diagrams, syntax highlighting,
sanitization, images, and fonts.

We thank these projects and their maintainers. Exact dependencies and
versions are recorded in the package manifests and pnpm-lock.yaml;
third-party components retain their upstream copyrights and licenses.
README.md also acknowledges the optional inference and tool integrations
that operators can connect to Clio.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Pinned external tools

Clio Coder does not bundle the programs below. `clio-coder tools install
<id>` downloads a pinned upstream release on request, verifies it against
the checksum recorded in src/domains/toolchain/registry.ts, and places the
upstream license text beside the binary under the Clio data directory. Each
program remains under its own license and copyright; Clio neither modifies
nor redistributes it.

herdr (https://herdr.dev, https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr)
  Copyright the herdr authors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Used as the terminal multiplexer behind Clio panes.

yazi (https://yazi-rs.github.io, https://github.com/sxyazi/yazi)
  Copyright the yazi authors.
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used as the terminal file manager behind the file-picker pane.

croc (https://schollz.com/software/croc6, https://github.com/schollz/croc)
  Copyright Zack Scholl and the croc authors.
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Used as the relay file-transfer backend for machine-to-machine transfers.

